# Release data and locale strings self-heal (hard rule)

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-08-18): **distribution data that ships with a
release must load itself if missing after upgrade.** The same pattern applies
to UI locale strings.

> **Shipping catalogs, seed packs, and reference dictionaries that land in a
> release must self-heal when missing or empty after upgrade. Operator-visible
> one-time configuration (toast + progress + what was done), then serve the
> data. 400-on-missing-distribution-data is forbidden. Empty-forever without
> heal is forbidden. Schema-only is not delivery.**
>
> **If a UI string is missing: reload that string once from the shipped
> locale catalogs. If it is still missing, show an on-screen error that names
> the string ID and log it. Do not invent a translation. Do not hide the gap
> with a silent English fallback.**

## 1. Catalogs / seed / reference packs

Applies to known-default-credentials, playbooks, locale packs, and any other
install-tree or embedded pack the MSI / `core-assets` already ships. Find the
existing pack — do not invent a second dictionary.

| Required | Forbidden |
| --- | --- |
| GET list returns **200** after heal (or 200 + empty **after** a failed heal with a visible error) | HTTP 400 because a shipped file or seed is absent |
| Heal from the product pack (installer / `core-assets` / embedded) | Empty-forever page with no heal attempt |
| Toast: one-time configuration is running; progress; then “Loaded … (N)” | Silent spinner-forever; lab SOP in the toast |
| Fail closed: visible error + Retry if heal fails | Silent drop ([`silent-failure-is-a-bug.mdc`](silent-failure-is-a-bug.mdc)) |

Worked catalog example: `GET /api/admin/known-default-credentials/sources`
must never 400 when `sources-manifest.json` is off the exe path. Heal or
return 200 + empty list + honesty. Catalog rows seed from the shipped pack.

## 2. Missing UI strings

Shipped catalogs: `core-assets/content/locales*`, SPA `ui/src/i18n`,
`pim-app-config-i18n`, server `locales/<tag>/`.

1. **Reload once** (in-session) from those resource files.
2. **If still missing:** on-screen error that names the **string ID** (key).
   Log (`tracing` / front-end logger). Do not invent a translation.
3. Do **not** show a bare key with no explanation. Do **not** silently
   substitute English in a loaded non-English pack (that hides the gap).
   US English **source** `defaultValue` on `en` remains the identifier path
   ([`enterprise-localization.mdc`](enterprise-localization.mdc)).

```text
// BAD — silent English in a German pack; gap invisible
t('knownDefaults.title') → "Known Default Credentials"

// BAD — raw key, no explanation
t('knownDefaults.title') → "knownDefaults.title"

// GOOD — after one catalog reload still missing
"Missing string: common:knownDefaults.title"
```

Agent drafts do not close localization-work items
([`localization-work-queue.mdc`](localization-work-queue.mdc)).

## 3. Agent duty

1. New or changed shipping reference data includes a heal path in the same
   change set (list GET + operator UX).
2. New SPA/server chrome keys land in US English source and DE in the same
   change set; missing-key healer stays wired.
3. Mirror this file to `core-assets/.cursor/rules/` 
   ([`auto-commit-push.mdc`](auto-commit-push.mdc)).
4. No lab hostnames, identities, or agent thinking in operator chrome
   ([`no-lab-config-in-operator-ui.mdc`](no-lab-config-in-operator-ui.mdc)).

